944 | ###########################################################################
945 | #
946 | # Workflow configuration
947 | #
948 | # The following properties map specific workflow steps to their associated approvers
949 | # The name of the workflow or decision is the part of the key after "jspwiki.approver.".
950 | # This is a logical name JSPWiki uses to determine which Principal to consult for approval.
951 | # The Principal is identified up by AuthorizationManager at runtime; it looks for a Principal
952 | # match as follows: GroupPrincipals; Roles; WikiPrincipals/other principals. Thus, if a value
953 | # of "Admin" is supplied JSPWiki will first check the GroupManager to see if group Admin exits;
954 | # then the container roles, if any; then, user Principals. If the value is blank or the
955 | # property is commented out, it means that the workflow does not require approval.
956 | #
957 | # EXAMPLE:
958 | # Uncomment the next line to require the Admin group (or Admin user, if a group is not found)
959 | # to approve wiki pages after saving.
960 | #jspwiki.approver.workflow.saveWikiPage=Admin
961 | 
962 | # Uncomment the next line to require the Admin group to approve new user profiles
963 | #jspwiki.approver.workflow.createUserProfile=Admin
