39 |    <!--
40 |       WikiServletFilter defines a servlet filter which filters all requests. It was
41 |       introduced in JSPWiki 2.4.
42 | 
43 |       In 2.7/2.8, the WikiServlet filter also performs an important security function:
44 |       it sets authentication status based on container credentials. It should generally
45 |       execute first. Note that if you configure a filter *before* this one that returns
46 |       non-null values for getUserPrincipal() or getRemoteUser(), WikiSecurityFilter
47 |       will pick the credentials up, and set the user's WikiSession state to
48 |       "authenticated." WikiServletFilter will also set the WikiSession's' state
49 |       to "authenticated" if jspwiki.properties property "jspwiki.cookieAuthentication"
50 |       is set to true, and the user possesses the correct authentication cookie.
51 | 
52 |       Lastly, if jspwiki.properties property "jspwiki.cookieAssertions" is set to true,
53 |       WikiServletFilter will also set WikiSession state to "asserted" if the user
54 |       possesses the correct "assertion cookie."
